+## [2026-09-26T01:57:40.482Z]
+Switching the reviewer used to leak the previous provider's API key. A key stored in yg-secrets.yaml outranks the provider's environment variable, and init rewrote only the committed reviewer section, so after a switch the old key was sent to the newly configured provider or endpoint while init printed that no key would be used. The flag path also copied a key it read from the environment into yg-secrets.yaml, which is how most such stale keys got there, and which made a rotated variable silently ineffective.
+
+Init now reads where the bootstrap tier sent its key before rewriting it, and afterwards settles the stored key: a typed key is written; a stored key is removed whenever the tier now points at another provider or endpoint, or when a key was chosen some other way this run (the variable exported, or the prompt answered), because it would outrank that choice; only a re-run for the same provider and endpoint with nothing else chosen keeps it. A key from the environment is never written. What init prints follows what happened — removed, kept (the reviewer will send it), or none — so the "no key" line is only printed when it is true.
